<title>FRANCE: Elf cuts stake in Technip to 3.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Elf cuts stake in Technip to 3.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elf Aquitaine has cut its stake in French engineering company Technip to 3.1 percent from 6.2 percent following the sale of 500,000 shares by Elf subsidiary Sogelfa, the French stock markets association (SBF) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The sale will be completed in the March account and will not change relative holdings of the other major shareholders. Isis controls 14.8 percent of Technip's capital, Gaz de France has 11.3 percent and Total 6.1 percent.</p>
<p>At the beginning of January, Sogelfa reduced Elf's participation in Technip to 6.2 percent from 9.35 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
